B) Take a number as input and print the multiplication table for it.

CODE :

import java.util.Scanner;
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println("Multiplication Table of " + n + ":");

        for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
            System.out.println(n + " x " + i + " = " + (n * i));
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}



OUTPUT :

Multiplication Table of 5:
5 x 1 = 5
5 x 2 = 10
5 x 3 = 15
5 x 4 = 20
5 x 5 = 25
5 x 6 = 30
5 x 7 = 35
5 x 8 = 40
5 x 9 = 45
5 x 10 = 50


C)  Take 2 numbers as inputs and find their HCF and LCM. 

CODE : 

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter first number: ");
        int a = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.print("Enter second number: ");
        int b = sc.nextInt();

        int x = a;
        int y = b;


        while (y != 0) {
            int temp = y;
            y = x % y;
            x = temp;
        }

        int hcf = x;
        int lcm = (a * b) / hcf;

        System.out.println("HCF = " + hcf);
        System.out.println("LCM = " + lcm);

        sc.close();
    }
}

OUTPUT :

Enter first number: 1
Enter second number: 2
HCF = 1
LCM = 2

